sec.p:
In our data analysis, we first estimated the probability of all possible level 3 and level 1 dimension combinations under independence, based on multiplication of the marginal frequencies of the levels per dimension using the following formula:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\text{Probability (D1}}\_{\text{L1}}|{\text{ D2}}\_{\text{L3)}}\,=\,{\text{prevalence (D1}}\_{\text{L1)}} \times {\text{prevalence (D2}}\_{\text{L3)}},$$\end{document}Probability (D1_L1|D2_L3)=prevalence (D1_L1)×prevalence (D2_L3),where D1_L1 is dimension 1 (e.g., mobility) level 1 and D2_L3 is dimension 2 (e.g., self-care) level 3.
